# Files excluded from `git archive` release tarballs (make dist).
# apt/ and web/ are published-website content, not source: they belong on
# GitHub Pages, not in a source release.  (ci.yml's dist guard also caps the
# tarball at 2 MB — it reached 6.1 MB at v1.7 by shipping the apt pool.)
#
# .github/ IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED HERE.  GitHub's own source tarball
# (api.github.com/repos/.../tarball) honours export-ignore, and OpenSSF
# Scorecard analyses the repository by fetching exactly that tarball — so
# excluding .github/ made all eight workflow files invisible to it.  That cost
# four checks at once: Dangerous-Workflow ("no workflows found", and it is the
# single heaviest check), Token-Permissions ("No tokens found"),
# Pinned-Dependencies ("no dependencies found") and SAST ("no SAST tool
# detected", because CodeQL is detected by reading the workflow).  Shipping CI
# configuration in a source tarball is normal and costs ~30 KB.
.gitignore      export-ignore
.gitattributes  export-ignore
apt/            export-ignore
web/            export-ignore
